# Line endings are normalized to LF in the repository, and land in the working tree
# in whatever form is native to the developer's system. Without this file the line endings
# are decided by the local core.autocrlf setting: on Windows the tree ended up CRLF,
# on Linux and in CI — LF, and `format:check` with a hard-coded `endOfLine` failed on every
# file at once — not because the formatting diverged, but because the environment is different.
* text=auto

# Binary — do not touch at all: normalization would corrupt the contents.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pfx binary
